-- title:
--   Finiteness of p-torsion in Pic⁰ in characteristic p
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, $K$ algebraically closed, and let $p$ be a prime number (a prime-ness fact instance) such that $K$ has characteristic $p$. Assume $F/K$ is separably generated by one transcendental element: there exists $x \in F$ transcendental over $K$ with $F$ finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $x$. Assume further that $F/K$ carries the curve package [`AlgebraicCurve.IsCurveOver`](def/AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver.html#L15), namely: for every nonzero $f \in F$ there is a finitely supported integer-valued function $D$ on the places of $F/K$ (a place being a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring) with $D(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v f$ for all $v$ and of total degree $0$; each residue field of a place is finite-dimensional over $K$; and $\Omega_{F/K}$ is free of rank one over $F$. Assume $F$ is of essentially finite type over $K$, and that [`AlgebraicCurve.HasCanonicalDivisor`](def/AlgebraicCurve_CanonicalDivisor.html#L14) holds: every nonzero $\omega \in \Omega_{F/K}$ has a finitely supported divisor $D$ with $D(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v$ of the differential coefficient of $\omega$ at $v$, for all places $v$. Then the $p$-torsion subgroup of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(F/K)$, the quotient of the group of degree-zero divisors by the principal ones, is a finite type.
--
--   This is the prime case of the classical finiteness of the $p$-primary torsion of the Jacobian of a curve over an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, equivalently the statement that the $p$-rank (Hasse–Witt invariant) is finite, bounded by the genus. It is the base of an induction and is cited by [`AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.finite_torsion_pow_char`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.finite_torsion_pow_char), which treats the powers $p^n$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Pic0_finite_torsion_char.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver
